@* Exercise 080 - Dynamic Component Parameter Mapping (advanced).
   Goal:   Turn untyped name/value text - a query string, a CMS record, a config
           file - into a parameter dictionary a <DynamicComponent> will accept.
   Drills: reflecting over a component's [Parameter] properties, converting values
           to their declared types, and refusing what does not fit instead of
           letting DynamicComponent throw at render time.
   Passes: dotnet test --filter FullyQualifiedName~Ex080_ *@

@* TODO: render a <DynamicComponent> for ComponentType, handing it the dictionary
   that OnParametersSet built. *@

@code {
    [Parameter] public Type ComponentType { get; set; } = typeof(DynamicBadge);

    /// Raw text, as it would arrive from outside the app.
    [Parameter] public IReadOnlyDictionary<string, string> RawValues { get; set; }
        = new Dictionary<string, string>();

    /// One line per raw entry that could not be mapped. Order follows RawValues.
    public IReadOnlyList<string> Problems { get; private set; } = [];

    public const string UnknownParameter = "unknown parameter";
    public const string NotConvertible = "not convertible";

    // TODO: build the dictionary <DynamicComponent> is handed, and the Problems list
    // beside it. For each entry of RawValues, matching by exact name:
    //   - the target type has a public property with that name AND a [Parameter]
    //     attribute -> convert the text to the property's type and include it.
    //     Convert against CultureInfo.InvariantCulture; a plain string needs no
    //     conversion at all.
    //   - no such property, or a property that is public but NOT a [Parameter]
    //     -> "<name>: unknown parameter", and leave it out.
    //   - the text does not convert -> "<name>: not convertible", and leave it out.
    // Leaving a bad entry in is not an option: DynamicComponent throws on a name the
    // target does not declare, which takes the whole render down instead of the one
    // value that was wrong.
    // Do the mapping here, once per parameter push, rather than from the markup -
    // a render expression that assigns Problems writes state while rendering it.
    protected override void OnParametersSet()
        => throw new NotImplementedException("TODO: Ex080 - map the raw values onto the component's parameters");
}
